{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773165994,"nonce":"V36LLNHO9bhKR3r1M0bOJX5FdAA=","title":"Worker hardcodes mechanics: N_MUSCLES=6, OBS_DIM=17, AnalyticalMusculoskeletalPlant always used regardless of graph","message":"The training worker in app.py ignores the mechanics node type when building the plant. It always constructs AnalyticalMusculoskeletalPlant with default_6muscle_2link_topology(), hardcodes N_MUSCLES=6, N_JOINTS=2, OBS_DIM=17, and uses a midpoint body preset — none of which are read from the graph spec.\n\nThe fix requires:\n1. Dispatch on mechanics node type (TwoLinkArm, Arm6MuscleRigidTendon, PointMass8MuscleRelu, etc.)\n2. Read mechanics params from graph node (dt, body dimensions, muscle params)\n3. Derive OBS_DIM from graph topology rather than hardcoding\n4. Eventually read Arm6MuscleRigidTendon subgraph nodes to build the muscle pipeline\n\nThis is the largest remaining graph-as-model violation. Lower urgency since the current hardcoded defaults produce correct training for the default graph layout, but any graph deviation silently produces the wrong model.","files":null}]}